course: dictionary
lesson: 12585
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. These are its context, and they give you clues. «A dipper bobbed up and down on a rock by the fast stream.» Here, the stream and the rock tell you a dipper is a living thing, a small bird.
explain: «Use the dipper to scoop water from the bucket.» The bucket and the water tell you this dipper is an object, a ladle with a long handle. The same word, but a different meaning, because the context is different.
explain: «We screamed on every drop of the big dipper at the fair.» Screamed, drop and fair are the clues. This is a fairground ride, a roller-coaster. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so always check the context.
fact: A dipper can be a small bird that dives in fast streams to catch insects.
fact: A dipper can also be a ladle with a long handle for scooping water.
fact: «The Big Dipper» is a group of stars shaped like a ladle. In the UK it is called the Plough.
fact: At the seaside or a fair, «a big dipper» is a roller-coaster ride.
exercise: «A dipper bobbed up and down on a rock by the fast stream.» What is a dipper here? | *A small bird that dives in streams | A fairground ride | A group of stars | A ladle with a long handle
exercise: «Use the dipper to scoop water from the bucket.» What is a dipper here? | A roller-coaster ride | A small bird that catches insects | A group of stars | *A ladle with a long handle
exercise: «We looked up at the Big Dipper and found the North Star.» What does the Big Dipper look like? | A bucket of water | A ride at the fair | A bird with long legs | *Stars shaped like a ladle
test: «We screamed on every drop of the big dipper at the fair.» Which meaning fits best? | A bird that walks under water | *A fairground roller-coaster ride | Stars shaped like a ladle | A ladle for scooping water
test: In the UK, the Big Dipper in the sky has another name. What is it? | The Dipper Bird | *The Plough | The Milky Way | The Little Dipper
exam: «The ___ walked along the stream and dived under the water to catch insects.» Which word fits best? | ladle | plough | *dipper | Big Dipper
